      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "3. Human-consumable status reporting contract (STRICT)",
      "prov:value": "Formalized in cat-harness#1396 (2026-11-23): coordinator swarm updates must stand alone for a human reader outside the worker transcripts, banning naked worker codes, bare PR ranges, and unglossed work-item IDs, and requiring both the Live Repository Queue Scoreboard (PRs, Work Items, Issues) and the four-part Milestone & Epic Progress Rollups.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "cat-harness#1396",
        "2026-11-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-11-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/swarm-monitor.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "4. Worker health, memory/swap saturation, and Andon-cord triage",
      "prov:value": "Production lesson recorded in cat-harness#1396 (2026-11-23): on macOS and swap-backed Linux, ps -o rss hides runaway memory leaks once pages are compressed or swapped out (for example into /System/Volumes/VM/swapfile*), silently exhausting root disk space (ENOSPC) while resident memory per process remains under 3 GB. Every monitor sweep inspects total memory plus compressed/swap usage alongside df -h / and SIGKILLs runaway subprocesses immediately.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "cat-harness#1396",
        "2026-11-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-11-23"
      ]
    }
  ]
